          "html": "<section class=\"revealPart\" id=\"focus-paragraph-2-0\">\n<h3>完整原文 · 第2段</h3>\n<p>One in three Americans who are at least 40 have, or plan to have a job in retirement to prepare for a longer life, according to a survey conducted by Harris Poll for TD Ameritrade. Even more surprising is that more than half of “unretirees”—those who plan to work in retirement or went back to work after retiring—said they would be employed in their later years even if they had enough money to settle down, the survey showed.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"revealPart\" id=\"focus-paragraph-2-1\">\n<h3>意群划分 · 第2段</h3>\n<p>One in three Americans / who are at least 40 have, / or plan to have a job in retirement to prepare for a longer life, / according to a survey conducted by Harris Poll for TD Ameritrade. / Even more surprising is / that more than half of “unretirees”—those / who plan to work in retirement or went back to work / after retiring—said they would be employed in their later years even / if they had enough money to settle down, / the survey showed.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"revealPart\" id=\"focus-paragraph-2-2\">\n<h3>意群翻译 · 第2段</h3>\n<p style=\"line-height:1.8;color:#2563eb;font-weight:500\">三分之一的美国人 / 至少 40 岁的人 / 或计划退休后找一份工作，为更长的生活做好准备 / 根据哈里斯民意调查 (Harris Poll) 为 TD Ameritrade 进行的一项调查<br>更令人惊讶的是 / 超过一半的“未退休人员”——那些 / 计划退休后工作或重返工作岗位的人 / 退休后——甚至表示晚年还会就业 / 如果他们有足够的钱安顿下来 / 调查显示</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"revealPart\" id=\"focus-paragraph-2-3\">\n<h3>标准译文 · 第2段</h3>\n<p>根据哈里斯民意调查 (Harris Poll) 为德美利证券 (TD Ameritrade) 进行的一项调查，三分之一 40 岁以上的美国人已经或计划在退休后找到一份工作，为更长的生活做好准备。更令人惊讶的是，调查显示，超过一半的“未退休人员”（那些计划退休后工作或退休后重返工作岗位的人）表示，即使他们有足够的钱安定下来，他们也会在晚年找到工作。</p>\n</section>",
