          "title": "第4段 · 篇章精读",
          "html": "<section class=\"revealPart\" id=\"focus-paragraph-4-0\">\n<h3>完整原文 · 第4段</h3>\n<p>“That’s actually a pretty large effect for a pretty small intervention,” Schwitzgebel says. Psychologist Nina Strohminger at the University of Pennsylvania, who was not involved in the study, says she wants the effect to be real but cannot rule out some unknown confounding variable. And if real, she notes, it might be reversible by another nudge: “Easy come, easy go.”</p>\n</section>",
